## Proposed Changes

### Frontend (Angular)

#### [MODIFY] [auth.interceptor.ts](file:///d:/shivam/doctor-appointment-system/doctor-appointment-frontend/src/app/core/interceptors/auth.interceptor.ts)
- Modify the global error handler interceptor so that HTTP `401 Unauthorized` responses from any login/auth/registration endpoint (e.g., containing `/api/auth/`) do NOT redirect the user to the generic `/login` page. This ensures users remain on their role-specific login page (e.g., `/doctor/login` or `/admin/login`) and see the appropriate validation error.

---

### Backend

#### [MODIFY] [Program.cs](file:///d:/shivam/doctor-appointment-system/DoctorAppointmentSystem/DoctorAppointmentSystem/Program.cs)
- Subscribe to the static `EmailSender.EmailSendEvent` directly in `Program.cs` after building the app:
  ```csharp
  EmailSender.EmailSendEvent += (sender, e) => {
      Task.Run(async () => {
          using var scope = app.Services.CreateScope();
          var emailService = scope.ServiceProvider.GetRequiredService<IEmailService>();
          await emailService.SendEmailAsync(e.Email, e.Subject, e.Body);
      });
  };
  ```
- This completely avoids creating a new background service class and directly uses the existing `EmailService` scoped registration to handle background emails safely and asynchronously.

#### [MODIFY] Service Email Migration
- Replace all direct dependencies and calls on `IEmailService` in the following services with calls to the static `EmailSender.SendEmail(...)` helper. Where templated HTML emails are built, build the HTML body and call `EmailSender.SendEmail(...)`:
  - [AuthService.cs](file:///d:/shivam/doctor-appointment-system/DoctorAppointmentSystem/DoctorAppointmentSystem/Application/Services/AuthService.cs)
  - [ClinicService.cs](file:///d:/shivam/doctor-appointment-system/DoctorAppointmentSystem/DoctorAppointmentSystem/Application/Services/ClinicService.cs)
  - [AppointmentService.cs](file:///d:/shivam/doctor-appointment-system/DoctorAppointmentSystem/DoctorAppointmentSystem/Application/Services/AppointmentService.cs)
  - [AdminService.cs](file:///d:/shivam/doctor-appointment-system/DoctorAppointmentSystem/DoctorAppointmentSystem/Application/Services/AdminService.cs)

